    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "it's just hard to say if i can actually put that into words. i was reading this thing about how some artists believe the only way to truly capture the essence of mortality is to bridge the gap between the art and the actual act of dying. like, the ultimate performance is when the artist becomes the tragedy. does that sound too extreme? or is there something beautiful in that kind of finality?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
